5. Composition Algebra

Primitives compose:

[
P_j \circ P_i
]

but composition is generally noncommutative:

[
P_j \circ P_i
\neq
P_i \circ P_j
]

Example:

[
P_{\text{story}}
\circ
P_{\text{identity}}
]

means identity selects how a story is inhabited.

Whereas:

[
P_{\text{identity}}
\circ
P_{\text{story}}
]

means the story alters identity.

These are not the same operation.

Narrative-memory loop

[ S_{t+1}

P_{\text{memory}}
\circ
P_{\text{story}}(S_t)
]

A story is interpreted using memory, then becomes a new memory trace.

Symbolic compression loop

[ \sigma

P_{\text{symbol}}
\circ
P_{\text{story}}(S)
]

Later:

[ \hat{S}

R(\sigma,c)
]

Ritualized identity loop

[ S_{t+n}

(P_{\text{identity}}
\circ
P_{\text{ritual}})^n(S_t)
]

Repeated embodied action alters identity geometry.

