6. Semantic Control Equation

A general semantic update can be written as:

[ \frac{dx}{dt}

V_{\text{story}}(x)
+
\nabla \Phi_{\text{goal}}(x)
+
\nabla \Phi_{\text{identity}}(x)
+
\nabla \Phi_{\text{emotion}}(x)
+
K_{\text{memory}}(x)
+
U_{\text{attention}}(x)
+
\epsilon
]

where:

• (V_{\text{story}}): narrative vector field,
• (\Phi_{\text{goal}}): goal potential,
• (\Phi_{\text{identity}}): identity potential,
• (\Phi_{\text{emotion}}): affective potential,
• (K_{\text{memory}}): memory kernel,
• (U_{\text{attention}}): attentional control,
• (\epsilon): noise, novelty, and external uncertainty.

This is not proposed as a literal neural equation. It is a renderer-independent control abstraction.

