7. Pantheon Translation Atlas

The Pantheon should treat every artifact as a point in a translation graph.

[
\text{Story}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Math}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Code}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Diagram}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Ritual}
\leftrightarrow
\text{Organization}
]

A translation is valid when a selected invariant survives.

Let:

[
T_{A\rightarrow B}
]

be a renderer translation.

Then fidelity is:

[ F(T)

\frac{|I_A \cap I_B|}
{|I_A|}
]

A high-quality Pantheon artifact should include:

1. original rendering,
2. extracted operator,
3. invariant set,
4. alternate rendering,
5. reconstruction instructions,
6. provenance,
7. known losses.

