8. Crazy Lever Compress

Compression quality is not measured only by size.

Define leverage:

[ L

\frac{
\text{reconstructable semantic structure}
\times
\text{transferability}
\times
\text{generativity}
}{
\text{description length}
\times
\text{ambiguity cost}
}
]

A Crazy Lever Compress artifact maximizes (L).

The ideal compressed unit:

• is short,
• is memorable,
• points to a large semantic neighborhood,
• reconstructs reliably in context,
• transfers across domains,
• produces new valid inferences,
• retains provenance.

Fruit-to-juice pipeline

[
\text{Experience}
\rightarrow
\text{Story}
\rightarrow
\text{Pattern}
\rightarrow
\text{Operator}
\rightarrow
\text{Symbol}
\rightarrow
\text{Retrieval Key}
]

The purpose is not deletion.

It is regenerative compression.

